  "body": "## What happens\n\nPR #517 changes the meaning of the thread record field `finish_allowance`. It is now the finishing pass's own depth, and it is never 0 on a new record. The Tormach lathe post (`assets/posts/tormach-lathe.cps`) accepts a G76 record only when `finish_allowance` is the last step of its own ladder.\n\nAn operation that was generated before PR #517 has `finish_allowance` 0 in its cached record. The stale stamp (`crates/app/src/operation/stamp.rs`, `current_stamp`) hashes only the inputs and has no generator version. Thus the operation reads Fresh, and the Tormach post refuses it by name. The refusal is safe, but its message does not tell the user to regenerate the operation. The user cannot see the fix from the message.\n\nFound in the full review of PR #517 (https://github.com/NeoTech/Camcraft/pull/517#pullrequestreview-5910390160), note \"Old projects\".\n\n## Expected\n\nThe refusal tells the user what to do: regenerate the threading operation. Alternative: the stamp carries a generator version, so that such an operation reads Stale.\n\n## Done means\n\n- A Tormach G76 refusal for a record with `finish_allowance` 0 (a record cached before PR #517) tells the user to regenerate the operation.\n- A test posts such a record and asserts the text of the refusal.\n- The Fanuc post's behaviour for the same record (it writes `R0`, the output of main before PR #517) does not change in this issue.\n",
